      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Accessibility\n* the combobox bulit from plain <input /> has no inherent semantic,\nso we need to lean on ARIA role and keyboard convention\nto make component usable in screenreader and keyboard\n* <ul>/<li> for list system with role=\"listbox\" or role=\"option\"\n* aria-label for input (if there is no visible label tag)\n* role=\"combobox\" for input tag\n* aria-haspopup to indicate the element can trigger an\ninteractive popup element\n* aria-expanded indicate whether the popup element is current displayed\n* aria-live (result region) so screen reader can be notified\n* aria-autocomplete to descirbe the type of autocompletion\ninteraction model\n(single line value -- autocomplete == 'inline'\ncollection value -- autocomplete == 'list')",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Accessibility\n* the combobox bulit from plain <input /> has no inherent semantic,\nso we need to lean on ARIA role and keyboard convention\nto make component usable in screenreader and keyboard\n* <ul>/<li> for list system with role=\"listbox\" or role=\"option\"\n* aria-label for input (if there is no visible label tag)\n* role=\"combobox\" for input tag\n* aria-haspopup to indicate the element can trigger an\ninteractive popup element\n* aria-expanded indicate whether the popup element is current displayed\n* aria-live (result region) so screen reader can be notified\n* aria-autocomplete to descirbe the type of autocompletion\ninteraction model\n(single line value -- autocomplete == 'inline'\ncollection value -- autocomplete == 'list')",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
