    {
      "id": "wRM656DU2KlbV-ACu2gTF",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 380.5910104692392,
      "y": 2789.904638729512,
      "width": 490.5397033691406,
      "height": 50,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0u",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1183533130,
      "version": 103,
      "versionNonce": 296227018,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1781558700482,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Dynamic loading count (how to limit over fetching)\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Dynamic loading count (how to limit over fetching)\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "BKmH8TYuqbOy3lrV6L5sS",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 376.9362690751747,
      "y": 2895.278063367595,
      "width": 1222.8389892578125,
      "height": 475,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0v",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1398138570,
      "version": 1568,
      "versionNonce": 1447603542,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1781562730153,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "HTTP cache, deduplication, idempotency\n* Feed and single-post response should carry short-lived cache control header with an ETag, so revalidation round-trip\nbecomes a cheap `304 Not Modified` when nothing change\n* A stale-while-revalidate directive lets the client paint cached data immediately while a background fetch refreshes it,\nthis is ideal when user bounce from post detail page back to feed\n* In-flight request deduplication belongs in data access layer. If the composer fires two rapid reaction on the same post,\nuser navigates away and back before feed page resolves, layer should coalesce identical requests and cancel superseded ones\nvia AbortController. (library like TanStack query or Relay do this by default)\n\n\n* Write need idempotency key. (Post creation, reaction, shares can be retried by clients, by service worker after reconnect,\nor by proxy on flaky network, so server treat a key seen twice as same write) - Eg: generate key on client (UUID, \nidepotency-key header) at the moment user submits, not send time, so retries carry the original key\n* Other update endpoint\n   GET /post/{postId}\n   PUT /posts/{postID}/reaction\n   DELETE /posts/{postId}/reaction \n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "HTTP cache, deduplication, idempotency\n* Feed and single-post response should carry short-lived cache control header with an ETag, so revalidation round-trip\nbecomes a cheap `304 Not Modified` when nothing change\n* A stale-while-revalidate directive lets the client paint cached data immediately while a background fetch refreshes it,\nthis is ideal when user bounce from post detail page back to feed\n* In-flight request deduplication belongs in data access layer. If the composer fires two rapid reaction on the same post,\nuser navigates away and back before feed page resolves, layer should coalesce identical requests and cancel superseded ones\nvia AbortController. (library like TanStack query or Relay do this by default)\n\n\n* Write need idempotency key. (Post creation, reaction, shares can be retried by clients, by service worker after reconnect,\nor by proxy on flaky network, so server treat a key seen twice as same write) - Eg: generate key on client (UUID, \nidepotency-key header) at the moment user submits, not send time, so retries carry the original key\n* Other update endpoint\n   GET /post/{postId}\n   PUT /posts/{postID}/reaction\n   DELETE /posts/{postId}/reaction \n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
